        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:1",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:1",
            "text": "Hoh Xil, which means “beautiful girl” in Mongolian, is located in Yushu Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, Qinghai Province. With the absence of humans, Hoh Xil has preserved its primitive state. It’s one of the regions that humans have little knowledge of, thus preserving it as an untouched natural paradise（天堂）."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "Hoh Xil is a forbidden zone for human beings, but a paradise of life. The reserve is home to more than 200 animal species, of which at least 20, including the Tibetan antelope（藏羚羊）, are state-protected. The antelopes’ fame grew further after it became one of the 2008 Olympic mascots（吉祥物）."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "Hoh Xil stands as China’s largest world natural heritage site, maintaining a high-altitude （高海拔） ecosystem and iconic species of the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau. However, the ecological environment of Hoh Xil is delicate. In 2007, the reserve issued a statement, prohibiting all individuals from entering it illegally. In order for visitors to see the highland creatures, 34 special sightseeing stations have been established so far along the Qinghai-Tibet railway."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "The scenery here is extremely grand, with snowy mountains and ice- covered peaks, endless grasslands, blue skies and white clouds reflecting on the river surface, all creating a relaxing and pleasant natural environment. In July 2017, Qinghai Hoh Xil was added to the World Natural Heritage List."
          }
        ],
